3. When is an object eligible for GC?

Employee emp = new Employee();
emp = null;

Now:

The Employee object was created in the heap.
The reference is removed.
If no other references point to that object, it becomes eligible for garbage collection.

Another example:

Employee emp1 = new Employee();
Employee emp2 = emp1;

emp1 = null;
emp2 = null;

Now the object has no reachable references, so it becomes eligible for GC.

