What is transaction propagation? What is the default propagation in Spring? Explain REQUIRED and REQUIRES_NEW.
Transaction propagation defines how a transactional method behaves when it is called by another transactional method.

The default propagation in Spring is Propagation.REQUIRED.

REQUIRED (Default): Joins the existing transaction if one exists; otherwise, creates a new transaction.
REQUIRES_NEW: Suspends the existing transaction and starts a completely new transaction.

We use REQUIRES_NEW when an operation (such as audit logging) must be committed independently, even if the outer transaction fails.

Easy Remember:

REQUIRED = Join or Create
REQUIRES_NEW = Always New


