What is NoUniqueBeanDefinitionException?
This exception occurs when Spring finds multiple beans of the same type and doesn't know which one to inject.

Example:

EmailNotificationService
SmsNotificationService

Both implement NotificationService.

If we simply write:

@Autowired
private NotificationService notificationService;

Spring throws NoUniqueBeanDefinitionException.

We can resolve it using:

@Qualifier("emailNotificationService")
@Primary
Difference
@Qualifier → Choose a specific bean at the injection point.
@Primary → Make one bean the default choice.

Customer Service succeeds, Credit Service fails. How do you maintain consistency?
In a microservices architecture, each service has its own database, so a normal database transaction cannot span multiple services.

One common solution is the Saga Pattern.

Saga breaks a business process into multiple local transactions.

If one step fails, compensating transactions undo the previous successful steps.

Example:

Customer Service saves customer.
Credit Service fails.
Compensation removes or marks the customer record appropriately.

