FetchType.LAZY loads related entities only when they are accessed.

FetchType.EAGER loads the related entities immediately with the parent entity.

In production, I prefer LAZY because it avoids unnecessary database queries and improves performance.

I use EAGER only when the related data is always required.

JWT Authentication Flow
Ideal Answer
User logs in with username and password.
Spring Security authenticates the credentials.
On successful authentication, the server generates a JWT.
The JWT contains a header, payload, and signature.
The client stores the token and sends it in the Authorization: Bearer <token> header.
For every request, a JWT filter validates the signature and expiration.
If the token is valid, the request proceeds. Otherwise, the server returns 401 Unauthorized.

